==Albanian==

===Etymology 1===
Probably from {{der|sq|ine-pro|*meHndʰ-|*mn̥(s)-dʰh₁-}}. Compare {{cog|non|munda|t=aim, strive}}, {{cog|got|𐌼𐌿𐌽𐌳𐍉𐌽|t=look up}}, {{cog|goh|muntar|t=keen, eager}}, {{cog|grc|μανθάνω|t=learn}}, {{cog|lt|mañdras|t=alert, awake, smart, minxish}}.

Standard/Tosk variant of {{cog|aln|mûn|mûn(d)}}; [d]-sound lost among majority [[Gheg]] dialects due to [[nasal vowels]] (which do not exist in [[Tosk]]).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sq|/mʊnd/}}

===Noun===
* {{sq-noun|m|-|mundi}} {{i|Standard}}
* {{sq-noun|m|-|mûn(d)i|head=mûn(d)}} {{i|Gheg}}

# [[agony]], [[toil]], [[great]] [[effort]]
# [[arduous]] and [[hard]] [[work]] {{i|that pays off}}
# [[tribulation]], [[cause]] of [[trouble]] or [[suffer]]

====Derived terms====
{{col4-u|sq|{{l|sq|mundur}}|{{l|sq|mundje|g=f}}, {{l|sq|mundja|g=f}}|{{l|sq|mundim|g=m}}, {{l|sq|mundimi|g=m}}}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|sq|Muji}}

===Etymology 2===
Cognate to [[Arvanitic]] / {{cog|aae|mundënj|múndënj}}<ref>{{cite book |title=Albanische Etymologien: Untersuchungen zum albanischen Erbwortschatz (Albanian Etymologies: Studies on the Albanian hereditary vocabulary) |author=Bardhyl Demiraj, Peter Dayan |year=1997 |isbn=9042001615 |publisher=Editions Rodopi B.V., Amsterdam - Atlanta GA |page=281, 460, 452}}</ref> and {{cog|aln|muj|mûj}}. Lost [nd]-cluster among majority Gheg dialects (due to [[nasal vowels]]), while the [d]-sound in Tosk participle {{l|sq|mundur|mun'''d'''ur}} shifted to a [t] in Gheg {{l|sq|mûjt|mûj'''t'''}}.
Either from {{der|sq|ine-pro|*meHndʰ-||to pay attention, wisdom}} or {{der|sq|ine-pro|*magʰ-||can, to be able (to do)}}. Alternatively from {{der|sq|ine-pro|*men(s)-dʰ(e)h₂||to learn}}.
* According to [[Wikipedia|Gustav Meyer]] a cognate to {{cog|goh|muntar||awake, alert, fresh}} and {{cog|lt|mundrùs||cheerful, merry}} as cognates. [[Wikipedia|Norbert Jokel]] agreed with Meyer and added cognated {{cog|lt|mandrùs||high spirited}} and {{cog|sla-pro|*mǫdrъ||wise}}.<ref>{{cite book |title=Albanesische Studien III. Lautlehre des indogermanischen Bestandteile des Albanesischen |author=Gustav Meyer |year=1892 |isbn= |publisher=Carl Gerold's Sohn |page=64, 80}}</ref><ref>{{cite book |title=Etymologisches Wörterbuch der albanesischen Sprache |author=Gustav Meyer |year=1891 |isbn= |publisher=Trübner |page=291}}</ref><ref>{{R:sq:SAEW|page=58}}</ref> Going back to {{der|sq|ine-pro|*meHndʰ-||to pay attention, wisdom}}. From the same P-I-E-root:
*: → {{cog|gem-pro|*mundōną}}, {{l|gem-pro|*mundraz}} (→ {{cog|goh|muntar||awake, alter, fresh}})
*: → {{cog|grc|μανθάνω|gloss=to learn}} (→ reflecting on alb. noun {{l|sq|mund||agony, hard work, etc.}}. See etymology 1 above).
* According to [[Wikipedia|Eqrem Çabej]] and [[Wikipedia|Bardhyl Demiraj]] either a cognate to {{cog|el|μόγος||trouble, distress}} (cf. albanian noun {{cog|sq|mund||agony, hard work, trouble}}) or a cognate to {{cog|goh|magan||to be able}}.<ref>{{cite book |title= Studime etimologjike në fushë të shqipes |author=Eqrem Çabej |year=1976/1982 |isbn=978999563520699956352089994381717978999438171599927761379789992776131 |publisher=Tiranë Akad. e Shkencave e RP të Shqipërisë, Inst. i Gjuhësisë dhe i Letërsisë |page=357-358}}</ref><ref>{{R:sq:Demiraj|page=281-283}}</ref> From {{der|sq|sqj-pro|*māK(e)nT-}}, from {{der|sq|ine-pro|*magʰ-||can, to be able (to do)}}. From the same P-I-E-root derived:
*: → {{cog|sla-pro|*moťь}} (→ {{cog|cu|мошти||to be able}})
*: → {{cog|gem-pro|*mahtiz}}, {{l|gem-pro|*mahtuz}}, {{l|gem-pro|*maginą}} (→ {{cog|got|𐌼𐌰𐌲𐌰𐌽||to be able, have power}}, {{cog|goh|magan}}, {{cog|en|may}}). Cf. english {{l|en|maybe}}, german {{l|de|möglich||possibly}} with {{cog|sq|mundësi||possibility}} and active {{l|sq|mund}} switching its meaning from ''“can” to  passive “could, try, maybe”'' ({{l|sq|mundem}}).
* [[Wikipedia|Eric P. Hamp]] suggested to {{cog|lt|išmintìs||to be able}}<ref>{{cite book |title=Evidence for Laryngeals |author=Werner Winter  |year=1965 |isbn= |ocolc=603158404 |publisher=The Hague, Mouton |page=138 }}</ref> (cf. also {{cog|lt|išmėginti||try}} and {{l|lt|išmintìs||wisdom}}).
* [[Wikipedia|Vladimir Orel]] derived it from {{der|sq|sqj-pro|*manda}}. Cognate to {{cog|lt|mudà||possibility}}, {{cog|lt|mudúoti||to try, attempt}} and {{cog|sa|módate||to rejoice, be merry}}.<ref>{{R:sq:Orel|page=277-278}}</ref> Cf. meaning of {{cog|sq|mundësi||possibility}}, {{l|sq|mundim||trying}} and {{l|sq|mundoj||I try}} with the [[Baltic]] cognates.

